    "created_at": "2017-07-26T18:10:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-26T18:10:42Z",
    "body": "I think we should change this sooner rather than later. In Blink we're behind on implementing byte streams, but others have done so, and should be able to get these benefits---especially if we have interested consumers in the wasm space. Plus, I believe right now the spec is incoherent, as it tries to transfer SharedArrayBuffers, which causes a spec-level assert failure.\r\n\r\nI do think it's sad that this exposes data races, but I also agree that SharedArrayBuffers in general broke that seal, and we should integrate with them rather than wishing they didn't do that.\r\n\r\nI'll try to work on this when I get done with TC39 and some other work items...",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
