    "created_at": "2019-07-02T15:01:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-02T15:01:44Z",
    "body": "From what I've heard from @vasilvv, there's a lot of overhead with the current approach, enough to be problematic for APIs considering using them, so perhaps more cross-cutting changes could be justified with the goal of not creating garbage on each chunk, given that performance is the point of the lower-level API.",
