    "updated_at": "2023-03-27T08:06:08Z",
    "body": "Hmm. I think the idea of `SharedArrayBuffer` was to use the typesystem to encode this sort of guarantee. I.e., if you have a normal `ArrayBuffer`, you know you're safe; if you have a `SharedArrayBuffer`, you're unsafe.\r\n\r\nWhat motivates the desire to let the safety vary independently of the type, for this particular web platform feature? Note that wasm memory can be made shraed using `shared: true` in the `WebAssembly.Memory` constructor, and I suspect most wasm thread-using programs already turn that on.",
